 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The store holds sessions in the web process's memory
+([keep sessions in process memory](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-process-memory.md)). Request handlers use the shared
+`sessions` instance in [`larder/session_store.py`](../../larder/session_store.py).
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Restarting or deploying a web process loses its sessions and logs its members out. Deploy outside opening hours
+  to reduce disruption; members must log in again afterward.
+- Processes do not share sessions. Use one web process, or sticky routing to that same process, to keep a member's
+  requests together. Sticky routing does not preserve sessions across restarts.
+- The dictionary does not evict expired sessions. Expiry enforcement remains the caller's responsibility; a caller
+  must also arrange cleanup for a long-running process to keep memory bounded.
 
 ## Shaped by
 
-- [Keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
+- [Keep sessions in process memory](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-process-memory.md)
